  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 237 PM EDT Fri Oct 16 2026\n\n********Breezy and Cool Today********* \n\nWith frontal passage this morning, winds have been breezy out of the \nnorthwest. We hit our max temps this morning right before frontal \npassage, and will hit our mins close to midnight. Overnight lows \nwill be around 40. Expect spotty, light showers through the \nremainder of the day. \n\nA surface high pressure will build into the region on Saturday and \nthe low pressure continue off to the northeast. This tight pressure \ngradient will keep breezy conditions through Saturday afternoon \nbefore weakening. Skies will gradually clear by Saturday afternoon \nfrom northwest to southeast. Highs on Saturday will be in the mid-\nupper 50s.\n\n***********This Weekend's Chill***********\n\nSunday morning, temperatures will dip into the low to mid 30s, which \nwill bring frost and a chance for freezing temperatures. A Freeze \nWatch has been issued for Bluegrass counties. This may be upgraded \nto a Freeze Warning or a Frost Advisory in subsequent forecasts. \nAreas southwest of this Freeze Watch may be added to the potential \nfrost advisory. In the afternoon, highs will warm into the low-mid \n60s.\n\n*****************Next Week******************\n\nWe will remain under loose ridging and surface high pressure for \nmuch of next week. This means light winds, clear skies, and highs \ncreeping up into the upper 60s on Monday, 70s through the middle of \nnext week, and potentially scraping 80 in a few southwestern spots \nby the end of next week. Overnight lows will remain in the 40s for \nnext week. Northeasterly flow and dry air aloft may bring some \nchances for dry air mix down next week. If this is the case, we will \nsee drier afternoon RHs in the upper teens and low 20s. Should be a \nseasonable fall week ahead.",
